Pushbuttons on D8–D11
Active-LOW Digital Inputs & Floating Avoidance
Connected between the GPIO pin and GND. When released, an internal pull-up resistor pulls the pin to \(V_{\text{DD}}\) (3.3V / logic HIGH). When pressed, the pin is pulled directly to GND (0V / logic LOW). This prevents the pin from floating in a high-impedance state.


Internal Pull-Up Resistors
PUPDR Hardware Resistor Network
Microcontrollers include integrated ~40 kΩ pull-up transistors on chip. Activating them eliminates the cost, PCB trace routing, and assembly of 4 external pull-up resistors on the board.


Mechanical Contact Bounce
Physical Switch Contact Physics
When mechanical switch contacts slam together, microscopic metal spring leaves physically bounce for 5 to 20 ms before settling. Without debouncing, a single press would register as dozens of false security alarms!


3x Status LEDs (D2 to D4)
Push-Pull Output Stage
Configured as General Purpose Outputs (MODER = 01). High-side MOSFET drives 3.3V to illuminate the LED, and low-side MOSFET sinks to 0V when turned off.





2. Firmware Code-to-Concept Breakdown








Code Statement (Framework / Bare-Metal)
Week 3 Theoretical Concept
Deep-Dive Explanation




RCC_IOPENR_REG \|= (1U &lt;&lt; 0);
Peripheral Clock Gating (RCC)
In STM32 processors, peripherals are unclocked by default to minimize dynamic power consumption (\(P = C \cdot V^2 \cdot f\)). Enabling the clock in RCC powers the internal flip-flops of GPIO Port A.


GPIOA_MODER_REG \|= (1UL &lt;&lt; (pin * 2));
2-Bit Mode Configuration (MODER)
STM32 uses two bits per pin in MODER (00 = Input, 01 = Output, 10 = Alternate Function, 11 = Analog). The formula (pin * 2) calculates the exact bit offset for any pin.


GPIOA_PUPDR_REG \|= (1UL &lt;&lt; (pin * 2));
Pull-Up / Pull-Down Register (PUPDR)
Writing 01 into the 2-bit field enables the internal pull-up resistor, ensuring the input stays cleanly at +3.3V when no button is pressed.


!(GPIOA_IDR_REG & (1UL &lt;&lt; pin))
Input Data Register (IDR) Reading
Reads the physical logic state latched by the input Schmitt trigger. Since active buttons pull the line LOW, the inverted bit test detects a pressed switch.


delay(50); / software delay loop
Mechanical Debounce Filtering
Introduces a 50 ms stabilization window, allowing mechanical oscillations to die down before confirming the valid gate breach event.


GPIOA_BSRR_REG = (1UL &lt;&lt; pin);
Single-Cycle Atomic Pin Control
Directly alters the output state without performing a read-modify-write on ODR, ensuring complete immunity to interrupt race conditions.

